==Overview==
<tabber>
Unawakened=
{{#tag:tabber|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros|type=Unawakened
|'''General'''
* Immune to [[lava]].
* Not too hard to obtain, nor is it too expensive for most [[First Sea]] players {{Money|960,000}}
* Low mastery requirements.
* Can be good for grinding if enemies are grouped together and do not have high mobility moves (e.g. [[Raider|Raiders]] utilize [[Combat|Combat's]] old [Z] move, making them hard to grind with Magma since the damage over time cannot land).
* Moderately short cooldowns.

|'''[Z] Magma Clap'''
* Quick start.
* Decent and deceptively big hitbox.
* Decent damage.

|'''[X] Magma Eruption'''
* Decent hitbox.
* Drops puddles that are easily predictable to land, unlike the Awakened version.
* There is a bug/glitch where the puddles can stun [[Enemies|NPCs]] until they disappear, making it good for boss hunting and grinding if used properly, similar to [V] Magma Meteors.

|'''[C] Magma Fist'''
* Decent hitbox.
* Good range and stun.
* Decent damage and moderate damage over time.

|'''[V] Magma Meteors'''
* The player can use this move on themselves, making it a good tactic to escape a combo or a click combo by an [[NPC]].
* High damage and damage over time.
* The damage over time from the split projectiles can stack considerably.
* There is a bug/glitch where the puddles can stun [[Enemies|NPCs]] until they disappear, making it good for boss hunting and grinding if used properly, similar to [X] Magma Eruption.

|'''[F] Magma Floor'''
* Very good for grinding if Elemental Immunity is active.
* Cannot be cancelled even if the user takes damage from enemies (unless travelling into sea or grabbed by a move).
}}

{{!}}-{{!}}Cons=
{{Overview|Cons|type=Unawakened
|'''General'''
* Most of the moves have high end-lag and startup, so the player can be punished if they miss the moves or when using the moves.
* Most moves render the user immobile when being used, making them easily punishable.
* Most moves have a range or hitbox that is hard to hit moving or far-away enemies.
* Moves have slow projectiles and bad range, making them able to be easily dodged with [[Flash Step]] or even [[dashing]].
* All moves are either unusable or hard to use in air because of slow speed, small hitboxes and short range, making it completely unviable for aerial combat.

|'''[Z] Magma Clap'''
* Short range.
* Low damage compared to the other moves.
* Moderate startup.
* No damage over time unlike other moves.

|'''[X] Magma Eruption'''
* Short range.
* Tiny hitbox that can be punished if missed.
* Slight startup and end lag.

|'''[C] Magma Fist'''
* Easy to avoid.
* Slow speed.
* Hitbox is hard to hit moving or airborne enemies.

|'''[V] Magma Meteors'''
* Extremely weak at long range.
* High end-lag.
* Projectiles are slow, so it is hard to use on players and enemies that are moving, unless they are next to the user. 

|'''[F] Magma Floor'''

}}
}}

|-|Awakened=
{{#tag:tabber|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros|type=Awakened
|'''General'''
* Extremely high burst damage.
* Extremely versatile due to its many passives.
* Can walk on water after awakening at least one move.
* Really good at defeating players with big hitboxes like Buddha users or sometimes Dragon and other Transformation fruits if used correctly.
* Widely considered by the [https://www.roblox.com/games/2753915549/Blox-Fruits Blox Fruits] community as one of, if not the best fruit for [[Sea Events]] due to its ability to walk on water and its extremely high damage over time.

|'''[Z] Magma Shower'''
* Possibly the highest damage in the game out of all fruits if every tick of damage lands. (Other than [[Empyrean]]'s [Z] move fully held)
* Can easily drain [[Instinct]] dodges during aerial combat.
* Enemies loses their ability to dash and cancels their skills instantly when inside the puddles.
* Moderately fast projectiles.

|'''[X] Volcanic Assault'''
* Decent mobility move.
* Decent combo potential.
* High damage and leaves puddles.

|'''[C] Great Magma Hound'''
* Can grab and stun enemies, even when Instinct-tricked.
* Good for starting Magma combos.
* High damage.

|'''[V] Volcanic Storm'''
* Can disable the enemy's ability to dash and use skills.
* Extremely high damage especially if all of the projectiles land.
* Can [[Instinct/Break|break instinct]].
* The puddles take a long time to disappear, dealing high damage over time.

|'''[F] Beast Ride'''
* Decent damage when released.
* Cannot be canceled even if the user takes damage.
* Low cooldown.
* Decent flight speed for short distance travelling, such as from enemy to [https://blox-fruits.fandom.com/wiki/NPCs#Quest_NPCs quest-giver].
}}

{{!}}-{{!}}Cons=
{{Overview|Cons|type=Awakened
|'''General'''
* All moves are difficult to aim in the air, making it unviable for aerial combat.
* Most of the moves hold the user in place for a short time.
* The user can get stuck and drown if they flash step on water.

|'''[Z] Magma Shower'''
* Extremely hard to land outside combo or when the opponent is sky camping.
* Hard to hit mobile enemies.
* Hard to deal full damage especially on airborne or moving enemies.

|'''[X] Volcanic Assault'''
* Single target attack.
* High end-lag.
* Unlike the unawakened [X] Magma Eruption, this move cannot hit large objects, including The Leviathan and Sea Beasts. 

|'''[C] Great Magma Hound'''
* Cannot break Instinct if not connected to the ground.
* Low range and travel speed.

|'''[V] Volcanic Storm'''
* Extremely hard to land or hit when the opponent is sky camping.
* Easy to avoid from afar.

|'''[F] Beast Ride'''
* Relatively slow speed, especially when compared to other [[Blox Fruits|fruits']] [[flight]] skills.
* Travels slightly slower when the user's [[health]] is low.
* Has a time limit.
}}
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Unawakened Magma was reworked in Update 17.3, changing the ability visuals and generally updating them.
** The [[Magma Admiral]] and the [[Lava Pirate]] use the old, unawakened version of Magma.
* If a [[Boats|boat]] collides with a magma puddle created by a Magma user, it will immediately stop.
* Awakened Magma's {{Ability|F|1}} move uses the same sound effect as a [[Sea Beast]]'s roar.
* Awakened {{Ability|Z|1}} has an incredible range, as the projectiles do not despawn even at 2500+ meters.
* The Scorching Puddles reappear and disappear faster when the player is holding a move.

